From 1eb2474ec95029e3d0d8a36463348b894f133e60 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vagif96 <a.vaqif96@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:05:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] qualcommax: ipq50xx: add support for TP-Link Archer AX55 v4

The Archer AX55 v4 is the same board as the Archer AX55 v1. Checked
against the stock v4 firmware (1.1.3 Build 20251030 rel.63052):

- SoC: IPQ5018 (MP03.3 reference design, same DDR CDT)
- NAND: 128 MiB, identical partition table (rootfs/rootfs_1/tp_data)
- Switch: RTL8367S over a 2.5G HSGMII link, reset on GPIO33
- GPIOs: buttons 25/31, LEDs 10/11/13/18/22/38/39, USB VBUS 27
- Wi-Fi: IPQ5018 2.4 GHz + QCN6122 5 GHz, board IDs 0x24/0x60,
  pre-cal in 0:ART at 0x1000/0x26800

The only difference is retuned Wi-Fi board data, so v4 has its own
calibration variant and ipq-wifi package, with board-2.bin files built
from the stock bdwlan.b24 and qcn6122/bdwlan.b60.

Not yet tested on hardware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EFTv5G5EUAjQfjYfRG5dBt
